.TH REBOOT 8 2026-09-25 "Substrate" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
reboot \- restart the system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reboot
.RB [ \-f ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default
.B reboot
sends
.B SIGUSR2
to
.BR init
(process 1), which performs an orderly shutdown (see
.BR halt (8))
and ends by calling
.BR reboot (2)
with
.BR RB_AUTOBOOT .
.B reboot
returns as soon as the signal has been delivered.
If signalling init fails,
.B reboot
prints a warning and calls
.BR reboot (2)
itself.
.PP
The kernel resets the machine through the keyboard controller and, if
that does not work, by forcing a triple fault.
.PP
An effective user ID of 0 is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Do not signal init; call
.BR reboot (2)
with
.B RB_AUTOBOOT
directly.
Processes are not terminated and
.B /etc/rc stop
is not run, although the kernel still unmounts all file systems.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Init was signalled.
.TP
.B 1
.BR reboot (2)
failed (for example with
.B EPERM
when not run as root).
.TP
.B 2
An unrecognized argument was given; a usage message is printed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kill (2),
.BR reboot (2),
.BR halt (8),
.BR poweroff (8)
